## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design practical CAPA governance tied to real-time data flows and multi-tenant risk without overengineering.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model fields (id, tenant_ids, sink, data_classification, evidence, region, remediation_links, state)
- Region-aware lifecycle states
- Minimal REST API (POST /caps, PATCH /caps/{id})
- Metrics: recurrence_rate, MTTR, false_positives, containment_time per region
- RCA template and safe-canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express endpoints for CAPA creation
const app = require('express')();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => { /* create CAPA */ res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123' }); });
app.patch('/caps/:id', (req, res) => { /* update CAPA */ res.status(200).send({ ok: true }); });
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design for a real multi-tenant data routing bug with data residency risk, ensuring traceability from detection to verification and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, tenant IDs, and route metadata
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine with clear escalations
- Linked logs/traces in CAPA records for auditability
- Canary rollout and RCA templates with measurable metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal REST API skeleton for CAPA creation
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { evidence, tenantId, routeInfo } = req.body;
  // persist CAPA and link logs/traces
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123', status: 'open' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify false positives and tune thresholds across regions?
- What automated checks would prevent reintroduction of the misrouting in future deployments?

